From d6e85b5d5187ab17a26a04186fea78cfc486a944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:02:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] engine: the person's Stop on a child is held, and what they
 write next corrects the task

When the person stopped a child chat to steer it, the parent heard "the
person stopped it" at once, woke, and reacted mid-correction; the child
dropped off its wait as soon as they wrote to it, though it still worked on
the parent's task.

Now the person's Stop is held for two minutes (ZERON_STOP_HOLD_MS for
tests). A message they write to the child meanwhile corrects the parent's
task: the child stays on the parent's wait and its still-working note, no
stop is reported, and its end reports as usual. A Stop left standing
reports once the hold is out. An agent's Stop and Zeron cutting a run off
still report at once.

A turn the held Stop cut that settles again otherwise (its runtime killed
after it, a failure) reports as that stop, once, not as its own failure.
Once the person writes to the child other than to correct the task, it is
theirs: the end of what it does for them no longer reports to the parent.
